# ==== testbench deck (exact input given to ngspice) ====
| * tb_pnp_mismatch.spice -- sky130 substrate-PNP local-mismatch Monte Carlo
| * (issue #17: sim-harness port; adapted from sky130-bandgap's
| * sim/pnp-mismatch/, whose own testbench targets bandgap-core-specific
| * device sizes this repo's design does not use -- see the topology note
| * below).
| *
| * Confirms the ported harness's local-mismatch (MC_MM_SWITCH=1) AND global
| * process (MC_PR_SWITCH=1) Monte Carlo mechanisms both produce non-degenerate
| * samples against THIS repo's own PNP topology, per issue #17's own
| * acceptance criteria edge case. Deliberately NOT run through
| * sim/bin/corner-run.py: that runner drives one deterministic .op per PVT
| * point and has no notion of resampling a deck N times, which is exactly
| * what a distribution claim needs. Driven instead by
| * sim/pnp-mismatch/run_pnp_mismatch.py.
| *
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * sky130 mismatch mechanism (verified against the pinned PDK, not assumed --
| * identical mechanism sky130-bandgap's own sim/pnp-mismatch/ already
| * confirmed working on this same PDK pin)
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * In sky130A the per-instance mismatch terms live inside the device
| * subcircuits in libs.tech/combined/continuous/models_bjt.spice:
| *
| *   .subckt sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40 c b e mult=1
| *   .param mm_bf = {sw_mm_..._bf * mismatch_factor * MC_MM_SWITCH
| *                   * AGAUSS(0,1.0,1)/sqrt(mult)}
| *          mm_is = {sw_mm_..._is * mismatch_factor * MC_MM_SWITCH
| *                   * AGAUSS(0,1.0,1)/sqrt(mult)}
| *   ... is = '<W0p68L0p68 Is expr> * 0.13 * (1+mm_is)'   (area-matching scale)
| *       bf = '<W0p68L0p68 Bf expr> * 0.45 * (1+mm_bf)'
| *
| * The gate is MC_MM_SWITCH (local/intra-die mismatch) and, independently,
| * MC_PR_SWITCH (global/inter-die process Monte Carlo) -- neither is settable
| * from the deck itself: every plain corner section of
| * libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice sets both to 0, the `*_mm` sections set
| * MC_MM_SWITCH=1 (MC_PR_SWITCH stays 0), and the `mc` section sets
| * MC_PR_SWITCH=1 (MC_MM_SWITCH stays 0). The section name is therefore the
| * switch. This run script exercises BOTH: `tt_mm` for the local-mismatch
| * points, `mc` for the global-process point, `tt` for the control point
| * (which must return sigma == 0 exactly for both switches).
| *
| * AGAUSS() is evaluated per subcircuit *instance*, so separate instantiations
| * of the same subcircuit already draw independently -- no per-device
| * parameter plumbing needed. ngspice re-draws on `reset`, which is what makes
| * the control loop below a genuine Monte Carlo; `setseed` makes it
| * reproducible.
| *
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * Topology -- THIS repo's own PNP usage, not a re-run of sky130-bandgap's
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * Confirmed by grep across design/netlist/*.spice (issue #17 port time):
| * every PNP instance in this repo's design is
| * `sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40` (the LARGE fixed emitter size) --
| * design/bias_core.md's own device-mapping table explains why: sky130 ships
| * only two fixed PNP emitter sizes and the small one (W0p68L0p68) is not used
| * anywhere in this design, so sky130-bandgap's own small/large area-ratioed
| * mismatch pair does not map onto this repo's actual circuit. What this
| * design DOES have, in both bias_core and temp_core
| * (design/netlist/bias_core.spice, design/netlist/temp_core.spice): a single
| * PNP (`XQ1`) diode-connected c=VSS b=VSS e=<node>, and an 8-way PARALLEL
| * array of identical PNPs (`XQ8A`..`XQ8H`, same connection convention, all
| * eight emitters tied to one shared node) built as eight separate X
| * instances -- not one instance with `mult=8` -- exactly as
| * design/bias_core.md documents ("mult only scales the mismatch terms, not
| * Is, the identical quirk gf180's pnp_10p00x10p00 has"). This IS the real
| * 8:1-ratio PTAT ΔVBE core the design's own topology depends on, so this
| * deck reproduces it directly rather than inventing a device-size ratio this
| * design does not have:
| *
| *   (a) "identical" pair: two single-unit W3p40L3p40 devices at equal
| *       emitter current -- the pair-offset any single-unit leg in this
| *       design sees (e.g. XQ1 vs one leg of the XQ8x array, or XQR).
| *   (b) "array1v8" pair: one single-unit device vs 8 PARALLEL units sharing
| *       one node, fed the SAME total branch current as the single unit (so
| *       each of the 8 legs carries 1/8th the single device's current
| *       density) -- the actual XQ1-vs-XQ8A..H topology, where a shared
| *       mirrored branch current is split 8 ways. This 8x current-density
| *       ratio is what generates the real VT*ln(8) PTAT ΔVBE term the design
| *       depends on. The 8-parallel array's *combined* random Is deviation is
| *       the average of 8 independent per-instance draws, so its relative
| *       mismatch sigma is expected to land near 1/sqrt(8) of a single
| *       device's -- a real, falsifiable prediction of this exact topology
| *       (see run_pnp_mismatch.py's analytic_sigma()).
| *
| * Every DUT is diode-connected the way this design's PNPs actually are:
| * collector and base tied to VSS (=0 here), emitter driven by an ideal
| * current source, so VEB = v(emitter node). Subcircuit pin order is (c b e),
| * hence `X<name> 0 0 <emitter-node>`.
| *
| * Bias currents: 1 uA and 10 uA total branch current for both the identical
| * pair (per device) and the array1v8 pair (split 8 ways in the array leg) --
| * the same two rungs sky130-bandgap's own mismatch record used (its own
| * cross-reference: rungs of a 100 nA..100 uA half-decade characterization
| * ladder), kept here for cross-repo comparability. This repo's own
| * per-branch bias currents have not been characterized against sky130 models
| * yet (spec/porting-plan.md Sec4 item 2, not yet filed) -- these are
| * generic, round convenience points, not a claim about this design's actual
| * bias point.
| *
| * No supply rail exists in this deck: every DUT is referred to its own
| * emitter node and biased by an ideal current source, the same as
| * sky130-bandgap's own sim/pnp-mismatch/ (see that repo's tb_pnp_mismatch.spice
| * for the identical justification, which applies unchanged here).
| *
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * Inputs supplied by the run script (this deck is not standalone)
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| *   corner.spice  -- generated: `.lib <sky130.lib.spice> <section>` + `.temp`
| *   $mc_seed      -- ngspice variable, set from the generated .spiceinit
| *   $mc_runs      -- ngspice variable, set from the generated .spiceinit
| * The defaults below apply only if the deck is driven by hand.
| 
| .include corner.spice
| 
| * ---- identical pair: W3p40L3p40 x2, 1 uA ----
| Ia1a 0 ea1a 1u
| XA1a 0 0 ea1a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| Ia1b 0 ea1b 1u
| XA1b 0 0 ea1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| 
| * ---- identical pair: W3p40L3p40 x2, 10 uA ----
| Ia10a 0 ea10a 10u
| XA10a 0 0 ea10a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| Ia10b 0 ea10b 10u
| XA10b 0 0 ea10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| 
| * ---- array1v8 pair: single vs 8-parallel W3p40L3p40, SAME total branch
| * current shared 8 ways (matching bias_core's/temp_core's real topology:
| * XQ1 carries the full branch current alone, XQ8A..H share the same total
| * current 8 ways -- an 8x lower per-device current density in the array,
| * which is what generates the real VT*ln(8) PTAT term. Scaling the array's
| * current source UP by 8x instead (equalizing per-device current density)
| * would cancel that ratio to ~0 -- exactly the kind of mistake
| * run_pnp_mismatch.py's own signal_vs_sigma check exists to catch, not
| * silently accept. ----
| Ir1a 0 er1a 1u
| XR1a 0 0 er1a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| Ir1b 0 er1b 1u
| XR1b0 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b1 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b2 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b3 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b4 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b5 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b6 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR1b7 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| 
| * ---- array1v8 pair: single vs 8-parallel W3p40L3p40, SAME total branch
| * current shared 8 ways (see the note above) ----
| Ir10a 0 er10a 10u
| XR10a 0 0 er10a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| Ir10b 0 er10b 10u
| XR10b0 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b1 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b2 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b3 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b4 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b5 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b6 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| XR10b7 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| 
| .control
| if $?mc_seed
|   setseed $mc_seed
| else
|   setseed 20260825
| end
| if $?mc_runs
|   let nruns = $mc_runs
| else
|   let nruns = 300
| end
| set width  = 512
| set height = 100000
| let run = 0
| dowhile run < nruns
|   reset
|   op
|   let da1   = v(ea1a)  - v(ea1b)
|   let da10  = v(ea10a) - v(ea10b)
|   let dr1   = v(er1a)  - v(er1b)
|   let dr10  = v(er10a) - v(er10b)
|   let vr1a  = v(er1a)
|   let vr1b  = v(er1b)
|   let vr10a = v(er10a)
|   let vr10b = v(er10b)
|   print da1 da10 dr1 dr10 vr1a vr1b vr10a vr10b
|   let run = run + 1
| end
| quit
| .endc
| 
| .end

